You are an expert developer. We are verifying the code generated by LLM to fix the SonarQube warning titled " Overrides should match their parent class methods in synchronization " which has the following description:
When `@Overrides` of `synchronized` methods are not themselves `synchronized`, the result can be improper synchronization as callers rely on the thread-safety promised by the parent class.

Noncompliant Code Example
    
    
    public class Parent {
    
      synchronized void foo() {
        //...
      }
    }
    
    public class Child extends Parent {
    
     @Override
      public void foo () {  // Noncompliant
        // ...
        super.foo();
      }
    }
    

Compliant Solution
    
    
    public class Parent {
    
      synchronized void foo() {
        //...
      }
    }
    
    public class Child extends Parent {
    
      @Override
      synchronized void foo () {
        // ...
        super.foo();
      }
    }
    

See

  * [CERT, TSM00-J](https://wiki.sei.cmu.edu/confluence/x/gzdGBQ) \- Do not override thread-safe methods with methods that are not thread-safe

 

